  "haridwar": [
    "Haridwar weddings booked from our Rishikesh base are usually planned as a single travelling assignment rather than a standard local visit, so venue and season details matter more than they would for an in-town booking. Resort and destination-style venues around Haridwar often have their own preparation spaces, which we confirm with the property directly where possible, and lawn or outdoor venues need a weather-aware backup plan for the styling area. Peak wedding season brings more competing bookings across the wider Rishikesh region, so Haridwar dates during busy weeks should be confirmed with more lead time than an off-season date would need. Because the team is travelling specifically for the Haridwar booking, we also factor in road or transfer time when planning the arrival buffer — an earlier ceremony time generally means an earlier departure from Rishikesh. If the venue is unfamiliar to us, sharing photos or a location pin in advance helps us plan the right team size and equipment before the day itself, rather than adjusting on arrival.",
    "Choosing a package for an Haridwar wedding starts with the same questions as any booking — how many people, what level of detail for the groom, and whether the wider baraat needs full styling or a simpler coordinated look — but travel from Rishikesh adds planning time worth building in. Because the team commits to a specific date and route for a Haridwar assignment, package and quantity decisions are best finalised a week or two earlier than they would be for a local wedding, giving enough time to prepare fabric and confirm the final artist count. If your Haridwar celebration includes multiple functions across a short trip, a combined package covering all of them is usually more practical than booking each date separately. We're glad to talk through a realistic package once we know your approximate headcount, the venue type, and whether the wedding is a single day or a multi-day stay — share what you have so far and we'll take it from there.",
  ],
